---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Quick start
description: Run Aceit Kit Starter, make your first edit, and export a prototype as static HTML.
---

{% from "macros/section.njk" import renderSection with context %}

<section class="section" id="quick-start">
  <div class="container container--narrow starter-library">
    <h1>Start your prototype</h1>
    <p>Use Node.js 24 or newer, npm, Bash, and Perl. From your copy of the template, run:</p>
    <pre><code>bash setup.sh "My Project Name"
npm run dev</code></pre>
    <ol class="starter-steps">
      <li>
        Edit the headline in
        <code>src/_data/sections.json</code>
        . Save and check the preview.
      </li>
      <li>
        Change your palette in
        <code>src/assets/css/tokens.css</code>
        .
      </li>
      <li>
        Build with
        <code>npm run build:production</code>
        , then run
        <code>npm run build:standalone</code>
        to get flat HTML in
        <code>out-standalone/</code>
        .
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The
      <a href="{{ '/sections/' | site_path }}">section library</a>
      shows which files to edit and includes a self-contained Fieldnotes download.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{%
  set cta = {
    title: "Ready to build?",
    description: "Start adding pages and sections to bring your prototype to life.",
    buttonText: "Browse sections",
    buttonHref: "/sections/"
  }
%}
{{ renderSection("cta", "", cta) }}
